# Sublet for SQLite 3.53.3: memsys5 and the lookaside pool, in a Capstone domain.
#
# A diff against sqlite3-capstone.c as build-sqlite-capstone.sh produces it from
# the amalgamation (its sed lines are the platform's, not this port's).  The
# primitives are sublet.h beside this patch; the amalgamation includes it in the
# first hunk, and the build puts this directory on the include path only when it
# applies the patch.  Every hunk belongs to one class of the bookkeeping in
# nested-allocators-paper experiments/A7-ports.md:
#
#   I  interface: the block for a level that carves it arrives linear, under a
#      handle the level below keeps (sqlite3MallocLinear; the grant memsys5 is
#      given; the API that hands the pool over and reports the counters)
#   H  hierarchy: a primitive where the allocator carves, hands out, frees or
#      merges (sublet_handle and sublet_split at memsys5's split, sublet_take
#      at both allocators' hand-out, sublet_give at both frees, sublet_give_to
#      at memsys5's merge, sublet_carve at both initial carves)
#   M  metadata layout: what may no longer live in freed memory, because it is
#      revoked (memsys5's free-list links, its control bytes and one
#      capability per atom in the configured heap; the lookaside's free lists
#      and slot capabilities in a table beside the pool; the parent handles)
#
# What the port gives up: an application-supplied lookaside buffer
# (sqlite3_db_config LOOKASIDE with a buffer) is refused, it is not a linear
# block this level can carve; the SQLITE_DEBUG poison writes into a freed block
# are gone, the block is revoked memory.  The allocators' policies are
# unchanged: the same blocks split and merge, the same slots pop and push, so
# the free-to-reuse gaps of A1 are the same under the port (the profile gate of
# A8).  Apply with patch -F0 -p1 to the copy in the build directory, before any
# instrument's patch.
